LICENSING OF THE FILES IN THIS FOLDER
=====================================

There are two kinds of file here, and they are not under the same terms.

1. ChromIQ's own files
----------------------
`iso12647.json` and this folder's structure are ChromIQ's own work and are
covered by the project's licence, the GNU Affero General Public License version
3, the same as the rest of ChromIQ. A copy is in the LICENSE file at the root of
the project.

`iso12647.json` contains NO tolerance value of any standard. It ships empty.

2. Third-party reference data
-----------------------------
No third-party reference data is bundled today. When any arrives, it is governed
by the terms its rights holder stated, not by the licence above, and ChromIQ may
not relicense it.

The terms granted to ChromIQ are recorded in README.md beside this file, in the
words the rights holders used. In short:

  Fogra          use and unchanged redistribution, including in commercial
                 software, provided Fogra is clearly named as the source.
                 Naming a Fogra set is not a certification or an endorsement.

  CGATS          made generally available to the industry; free to use in
                 software. No further condition stated.

  ICC            redistribution is fine; altered data must never be presented
                 as the original.

  Idealliance    inclusion in and distribution with software, under any
  (PRINTING      licence, provided the profile is unaltered. Requires the line
  United          "GRACoL is a registered trademark of PRINTING United
  Alliance)       Alliance."

  ISO            NO PERMISSION. Reproducing the content of a standard inside
                 software needs explicit permission or a licence; a single-user
                 reading licence is not enough. No tolerance value of
                 ISO 12647-7:2016 or ISO 12647-8:2021 is in this folder, in any
                 file ChromIQ ships, or on any branch it is released from.

                 Said precisely, because a broader claim would not be true: the
                 standards' NAMES and clause citations are used, deliberately
                 and with the owner's decision behind them, and a superseded
                 commit on a documentation branch that once carried more than
                 that is still reachable by its hash until the hosting service
                 purges it. That is recorded in
                 docs/design/issue_182_answers.md rather than papered over.

Anyone adding a file to this folder has to add its source and its terms to
README.md in the same change. A data file without a credit beside it is a
licence breach waiting to happen, and three of the four grants above are
conditional on that credit existing.
